Manage optional Eshu components

Usage:
  eshu component [command]

Available Commands:
  conform              Run component extension conformance fixtures
  diagnostics          Read component extension diagnostics through the configured API
  disable              Disable an installed component instance
  enable               Enable an installed component instance
  extraction-readiness Explain whether a collector is keep-in-tree, an extraction candidate, blocked, or external-ready
  grant                Record a core-issued producer grant for a core-owned fact kind
  grants               List recorded producer grants
  index                Manage component extension index metadata
  init                 Scaffold a new component package
  inspect              Inspect a component package manifest
  install              Install a verified local component package manifest
  inventory            List component extensions through the configured API
  list                 List installed components
  revoke-grant         Revoke a recorded producer grant so emissions fail closed
  schema-versions      List core fact-kind schema versions or classify a collector fact version
  uninstall            Uninstall an inactive component package
  verify               Verify a component package manifest against local trust policy

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for component

Global Flags:
      --database string   Temporarily override database backend
  -V, --visual            Show results as interactive graph visualization

Use "eshu component [command] --help" for more information about a command.
